---
/* The "what these columns mean" explainer.
 *
 * Collapsed by default and deliberately so. The distinction it draws — that
 * being submitted and being indexed are different facts — is load-bearing, and
 * it was originally two always-open bordered panels above the table. It is a
 * thing you read once, not a banner that should own the top of the page forever,
 * so it became a <details> the moment it stopped earning that space.
 */
---

<details class="seo-explain">
	<summary>What these columns mean</summary>
	<dl>
		<dt>IndexNow</dt>
		<dd>
			Whether we told the engines about this URL. A <code>200</code> means received, not
			indexed — those are different facts. One push reaches Bing, Yandex, Seznam, Naver, Yep,
			the Internet Archive and Amazonbot.
		</dd>
		<dt>Bing / Google</dt>
		<dd>
			Whether the engine actually indexed it. Read from a separate API that is not wired up
			yet, so these stay <code>—</code> for now. Google has no URL-submission API at all, so
			it will only ever be a status column here.
		</dd>
		<dt>Sync now vs Resend all</dt>
		<dd>
			<strong>Sync now</strong> rediscovers pages from the sitemap and pushes only what is new
			or changed since its last successful push — the same rule the hourly cron uses, so
			pressing it twice is a no-op. <strong>Resend all</strong> ignores that rule; it is for
			the first seed only, because bulk-resubmitting unchanged URLs is what earns a host a
			rate-limit.
		</dd>
	</dl>
</details>

<style>
	.seo-explain { font-size: 12px; max-width: 92ch; }
	.seo-explain summary {
		cursor: pointer; color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 12px;
		padding: 4px 0; width: fit-content;
	}
	.seo-explain summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
	.seo-explain summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: 3px; }
	.seo-explain dl { margin: 6px 0 0; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
	/* Uppercase micro-label rather than bold body text: at 12px a weight change
	   alone did not read as a heading against the paragraph beneath it. */
	.seo-explain dt {
		color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 10px;
		text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em;
	}
	.seo-explain dd { margin: 2px 0 0; color: var(--text-dimmer); line-height: 1.55; }
	.seo-explain code { font-size: 11px; padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--hover); }
</style>
